---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_240",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 240,
  "text": "<p> [[745.7]] <b>212. LEIBNIZ AN ERHARD WEIGEL</p>\n<p> [[745.8]] [Hannover, Mitte] September 1679. [215.]</b></p>\n<p> [[745.18]] Ad Erhardum Weigelium, Septemb. 1679 </p>\n<p> [[745.19]] Dissertationem tuam <i>de supputatione</i> legi non sine magna animi voluptate et quod eam\n[[745.20]] mittere voluisti gratias ago. Quanquam enim nonnulla non satis assequerer, multa tamen notavi\n[[745.21]] praeclara et profunda. Eaque occasione Tibi proponam observationem meam quae ad institutum\n[[745.22]] tuum (tractas enim ut in titulo habes <i>de supputatione multitudinis a nullitate per unitates finitas\n[[745.23]] in infinitum collineantis ad Deum</i>) pertinere nonnihil videtur. Notavi nimirum primus atque\n[[745.24]] etiam demonstravi theorema sequens quod nulli inter arithmetica hactenus inventa cedere\n[[745.25]] visum est amicis. </p>\n<p> [[746.1]] Sumantur numeri progressionis Arithmeticae tum simplicis tum replicatae, quos vulgo\n[[746.2]] vocant Figuratos.\n[[746.3]] <c15> </p>\n<p> [[746.4]] <p>Ex his fiant fractiones, ita, ut numeri isti ordine sumti sint eorum nominatores, unitas vero\n[[746.5]] sit numerator et habebimus series sequentes totidem.\n[[746.6]] <c17> <p><zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <tab/><zl>1<ne>4<be> <zl>1<ne>5<be> etc. </p>\n<p> [[746.7]] Quarum serierum <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>15<be> etc. </p>\n<p> [[746.8]] infinitarum has<zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>4<be> <zl>1<ne>10<be> <zl>1<ne>35<be> etc. </p>\n<p> [[746.9]] deprehendi esse <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>5<be> <zl>1<ne>15<be> <zl>1<ne>70<be> etc. </p>\n<p> [[746.10]] <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>6<be> <zl>1<ne>21<be> <zl>1<ne>126<be> etc. </p>\n<p> [[746.11]] <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>7<be> <zl>1<ne>28<be> <zl>1<ne>210<be> etc. <tab/> </p>\n<p> [[746.12]] ^#1+ <tab/>^#1- </p>\n<p> [[746.13]] Summasinfinit. <zl>1<ne>0<be> <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> etc. </p>\n<p> [[746.14]] Nimirum summa hujus seriei infinitae <zl>1<ne>3<be> + <zl>1<ne>6<be> + <zl>1<ne>10<be> + <zl>1<ne>15<be> etc. est <+4> finita nempe <zl>1<ne>1<be> quemadmodum\n[[746.15]] facile si desideres demonstrare possum. Eodem modo summa hujus seriei infinitae <zl>1<ne>4<be> + <zl>1<ne>10<be>\n[[747.1]] + <zl>1<ne>20<be> + <zl>1<ne>35<be> etc. est etiam finita nempe <zl>1<ne>2<be> . Et ita porro. <+6> At summa seriei hujus infinitae <zl>1<ne>2<be> <zl>1<ne>3<be> <zl>1<ne>4<be> <zl>1<ne>5<be>\n[[747.2]] etc. est <zl>1<ne>0<be> quae quantitas est infinita, major scilicet quovis numero assignabili, quemadmodum\n[[747.3]] etiam demonstrare possum. Interim multo imo infinities minor est quam summa seriei hujus <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>1<be>\n[[747.4]] <zl>1<ne>1<be> <zl>1<ne>1<be> etc. Vides itaque inter illud <+4> infinitum ordinarium, quod in omnium unitatum collectione\n[[747.5]] consistit, et inter finitum, nempe unitatem, dari aliquid intermedium nempe <zl>1<ne>0<be> quod est summa\n[[747.6]] fractionum omnium possibilium numericarum, unitatem pro numeratore habentium, simul\n[[747.7]] sumtarum. </p>\n<p> [[747.8]] Unum adjicio, quoniam in limine dissertationis tuae exhibes demonstrationem principii\n[[747.9]] statici, me habere analysin quandam in hoc genere, cujus ope in hoc principium incidi a priori\n[[747.10]] supponens nondum me ipsum nosse: sed quaerere quaenam ad aequilibrium obtinendum\n[[747.11]] proportio distantiarum esse debeat. Eadem opera [inveni] demonstrationem quandam generalem\n[[747.12]] ex qua paucis variatis multas alias statim efformare possum, non Archimedeam solum, et\n[[747.13]] tuam, sed et aliorum, et inter has nonnullas quas nemo adhuc adhibuit. Pendent autem omnes ex\n[[747.14]] una eademque analysi. Analysis autem, ut a me intelligitur, ab Algebra longe differt, imo\n[[747.15]] Algebra nonnisi exiguum ejus specimen est. Nam et in ipsa Geometria video characteristices\n[[747.16]] genus quoddam excogitari posse, in tantum ab Algebra diversum in quantum Algebra ab\n[[747.17]] Arithmetica discriminatur, cujus ope directe et facile praestari multa possunt, quae Algebra aut\n[[747.18]] non aut non nisi per ambages difficillimas potest, [cujus] rei multa specimina habeo. </p>\n<p> [[747.19]] In cap. 2 (dissertationis tuae prioris) §. 1. n. 4. non satis intelligo quomodo velis subtrahi\n[[747.20]] punctum intimum. Nam exempli causa in semicirculo non datur punctum medium seu centrum\n[[747.21]] magnitudinis (quod satis mirabile est) etsi detur centrum gravitatis. </p>\n<p> [[747.22]] Multa dicis quae mihi perpulchra, et vera jamdudum visa sunt. Arbitror enim non tam\n[[747.23]] mentem nostram in res agere quam Deum ad ejus voluntatem; et mentes oriri ex speciali\n[[747.24]] quodam modo cogitandi divinae mentis; quin imo addo in omni mente esse quandam omniscientiam\n[[747.25]] sed confusam et potentiam in totum universum sese extendentem sed refractam;\n[[747.26]] prorsus quemadmodum in deliberando una consideratio aliam elidit. </p>\n<p> [[747.27]] In ratiocinatione Tua, qua Dei existentiam probare aggrederis quaedam notavi, quae mihi\n[[747.28]] explicatione opus habere videntur: ea inprimis difficultas removenda videtur quod spatium et\n[[748.1]] tempus magnam habere videntur analogiam et dividi posse proportionaliter, itaque quemadmodum\n[[748.2]] spatium ex punctis compositum intelligi non potest, ne quidem numero infinitis, ita nec\n[[748.3]] tempus videtur componi ex instantibus unde sequitur aliud esse durationem quam repetitionem\n[[748.4]] praesentiarum. </p>\n<p> [[748.5]] Scripta tua vix apud librario inveniuntur, ego certe frustra quaesivi: inprimis delineationem\n[[748.6]] artium Mechanicarum: itaque beneficio tuo potiri illis valde velim. </p>\n",
  "number": "212.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN ERHARD WEIGEL",
  "date": "[Hannover, Mitte] September 1679. [215.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:212. LEIBNIZ AN ERHARD WEIGEL [Hannover, Mitte] September 1679. [215.] Ad Erhardum Weigelium, Septemb. 1679 Dissertationem tuam de supputatione legi non sine magna animi voluptate et quod eam mittere voluisti gratias ago. Quanquam enim nonnulla non satis assequerer, multa tamen notavi praeclara et p...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>